WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.255
Maya sold a simple digital offer at seventy-nine dollars.

00:00:03.255 --> 00:00:05.787
The path matters more than the brand.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:09.043
This lesson is about case: maya-style first sale path.

00:00:09.043 --> 00:00:10.128
Worked digital example.

00:00:10.128 --> 00:00:12.660
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.277
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:16.277 --> 00:00:21.703
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.703 --> 00:00:25.682
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:30.384
Stay practical: map Maya path to yours before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:35.960
Her path: clear who, specific promise, warm outreach, discovery, soft close, then payment.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.194
Remember the objective: map Maya path to yours.

00:00:39.194 --> 00:00:43.642
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:48.494
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:48.494 --> 00:00:52.941
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:57.793
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:57.793 --> 00:01:00.623
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:00.623 --> 00:01:02.240
Feedback beats guessing alone.

